# Teaching workspace — what does NOT belong in version control.
#
# The rule of thumb: this repo holds what we *authored* (lessons, reference
# docs, research, code, operating rules). Source material we merely *read* is
# either someone else's repo or someone else's copyrighted book — neither
# belongs here.

# --- Any vendored copy of the upstream skills repo -------------------------
# The subject under study is https://github.com/mattpocock/skills. Read it from
# a clone outside this workspace (../skills) — never vendor it in here.
#
# This entry is a backstop, kept deliberately even though no such directory
# currently exists: a clone carries its own `.git`, so git would record it as
# an embedded repository (a gitlink) that tracks no contents and emits the
# "you've added another git repository" warning. See CLAUDE.md.
skills/

# --- Books and other copyrighted source material ---------------------------
# Read for citation, never redistributed. Quotes live in the lessons with
# page numbers; the book itself stays out of the repo.
*.pdf
*.epub
*.mobi
*.azw3
*.djvu

# --- Windows / WSL interop junk --------------------------------------------
# Alternate data streams that ride along when files are copied from Windows.
*:Zone.Identifier

# --- OS junk ---------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Java ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Examples run via `java File.java` (single-file source mode, no build step),
# but an accidental `javac` would litter these.
*.class
code/**/out/
code/**/target/

# --- Editors ---------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- Scratch ---------------------------------------------------------------
scratch/
tmp/
*.log
